sensors: t41: gc5603: fix the doubled source path

DIR already ends in the sensor name and SRCS appends it again, so the
build looks for

    sensors/t41/gc5603/gc5603/gc5603.c

while the file is at sensors/t41/gc5603/gc5603.c, and make stops with
"No rule to make target .../gc5603/gc5603/gc5603.o".

The intended form is DIR=sensors/$(SOC), which is what t20/sp2307/Kbuild
- the one Kbuild in this repo that is not affected - still has. In every
other sensor Kbuild the sensor name was added to DIR without being
removed from SRCS. No sensor directory anywhere in the tree contains a
nested directory of the same name, so this affects all 257 sensor
Kbuilds across every SoC, not just T41; only the one this board needs is
changed here.

Upstream: https://github.com/openipc/openingenic

Signed-off-by: Oskari Rauta <oskari.rauta@gmail.com>

diff --git a/kernel/sensors/t41/gc5603/Kbuild b/kernel/sensors/t41/gc5603/Kbuild
index ddd87cf..65c5785 100644
--- a/kernel/sensors/t41/gc5603/Kbuild
+++ b/kernel/sensors/t41/gc5603/Kbuild
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 MODULE_NAME := sensor_gc5603_$(SOC)
 OUT := $(MODULE_NAME)
 
-DIR=sensors/$(SOC)/gc5603
+DIR=sensors/$(SOC)
 
 SRCS := $(DIR)/gc5603/gc5603.c
 
